<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Paris</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Parisian</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Paris is the capital of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> and has long been one of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>'s principal political and cultural centres. It was the seat of government of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/french-colonial-empire">French Empire</a> and the site of treaties such as the Treaty of Paris of 1763, which confirmed British colonial dominance. Its university was an early centre for the study of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-law">Roman law</a>, and the last Brazilian emperor, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pedro-ii-of-brazil">Pedro II</a>, died in exile there.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/paris.jpg" alt="Paris" width="320" height="200" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Yann Caradec from Paris, France · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:La_Tour_Eiffel_vue_de_la_Tour_Saint-Jacques,_Paris_ao%C3%BBt_2014_(2).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
